From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Demitri Nava <demitri@boltz.bio>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:24:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] buck2_events: start every BES stream with its command, and
 honour a command's PATTERN

When a command's ReSession or TargetCfg reached the converter before its
CommandStart, which the sink's worker can deliver out of order, the stream
began with a Started for an "unknown" command and a BuildMetadata holding
only those keys. BuildBuddy then reported a GitHub commit status for it,
before the command's own metadata said not to, and left it pending
forever. A command run on an argfile also showed `@/path/to/argfile` as
its pattern.

The converter now holds ReSession and TargetCfg until the stream has
started, sends the command's BuildMetadata straight after Started as Bazel
does, ahead of anything held, and takes a command's PATTERN metadata, when
set, as its patterns instead of its arguments.
---
 app/buck2_events/src/sink/bazel_converter.rs | 146 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 140 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

